This document assembles the official Riemann reference, P.B.F. derivation, recorded computational controls, relational connection, and final comparison into the complete submitted function chain.It preserves the distinct origins of the compared positions and the declared scopes of the computational results.The Riemann Hypothesis states:
The nontrivial zeros of have a real part equal to .
The condition supplied by this formulation is:This is the official reference position used in the comparison.The P.B.F. construction begins from the complete, internally undifferentiated whole .Equal binary division establishes:The two positions are equal in value. Halving one of them while preserving the other produces:The first operational value differentiation is expressed through:Within the P.B.F. construction, the complete differentiation establishes:and identifies:Regrouping the established parts gives:The complementary relation is:within the preserved whole.K.6 consists of two self-contained programs.Exact rational arithmetic controls the relations:The five substantive controls, their aggregate control, and the global result record PASS within the program's declared scope.The Binary Pulse remainder relation is executed through positions – using exact rational arithmetic.The recorded result is:POSITION_FIRST=0
POSITION_LAST=99
POSITION_COUNT=100
PASS_COUNT=100
FAIL_COUNT=0
FIRST_DEVIATION=NONE
GLOBAL_STATUS=PASS
K.7 executes one continuous sequential positional genealogy through the declared domain ending at .Genealogical state is preserved across consecutive segment boundaries and checkpoints. Internal genealogical references generate each P.B.F. positional segment, while an external base reference is constructed separately.The comparison order is:
Establish the external base reference.
Generate the P.B.F. positional segment from its preserved internal genealogical state.
Construct the comparison bitmap for the corresponding segment.
Compare the generated result and comparison bitmap byte-for-byte.
Within the executed domain, the recorded results report:
exact positional identity at every declared milestone;
zero false positives;
zero false negatives;
exact agreement with the separately calculated observation-count formula;
no first deviation;
global PASS;
maximum executed genealogy status PASS.
These results apply to the executed domain.K.8 contains three controls with distinct functions and separately recorded results.Two separately implemented P.B.F. and Binary Pulse operational paths are compared through the declared domain ending at .The implemented-state comparison includes:
candidate fields;
projected-hit structures;
state classifications;
closure sequences;
observation counts;
closure counts;
reproduced-position counts.
The recorded execution reports every operator-identity condition as PASS, operator identity as PASS, and first deviation as NONE.The validator, version 2.1.0, uses exact rational arithmetic to preserve:through eight binary-scale levels.Between adjacent levels, the numerator and denominator of all three fraction families are multiplied by two.The recorded result is:LEVEL CONTROLS: 8/8 PASS
ADJACENT TRANSITIONS: 7/7 PASS
GLOBAL STATUS: PASS
The rational source states are:The validator constructs exact Fraction values, projects them into finite Base-10 representations, and reconstructs their exact rational source values.The projection preserves and compares decimal representations produced by equivalent binary-scale expressions.The recorded result is:PROJECTION LEVELS: 8/8 PASS
CROSS-LEVEL REPRESENTATION IDENTITY: PASS
BASE-10 PROJECTION LOCK: PASS
The complete submitted function chain is:The computational components appear in presentation order; this does not define a software dependency between them.The left-hand position in the final comparison represents the independently derived P.B.F. half-function. The right-hand position represents the real-part condition stated by the Riemann Hypothesis.The relational connection brings these positions into comparison while preserving their respective origins.Rp9 black 📁 RP9. THE RIEMANN SUBMISSION
